    "created_at": "2024-01-25T06:30:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-25T06:30:54Z",
    "body": "Throwing at the IDL layer would change the exception for everything calling into StructuredSerializeWithTransfer at least. Not sure that's really possible. My idea was to add one-off checks and also to assert that the buffer is not detached in various IDL algorithms so callers are \"forced\" to deal with it.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
